    "note": "Oct 9 audit (Judy feedback: pointing that made no sense). Each clip is classified for conversation: centred (moving hands stay in front of the body, between hips and chest), neutral, or excluded as directional (pointing, indicating a side, behind or across), turn (torso or head turned away from V) or sweep (broad or overhead arms). Name rules first, then the measured shape (assets/gestures/clip-shape.json, scripts/Measure-GestureShape.py) on every rig that has the clip; excluded clips keep their workspot sequence (the probe can still play them) but never play in conversation.",
    "names": [
      [
        "point",
        "directional",
        "points (by name)"
      ],
      [
        "describe_(left|right|back)",
        "directional",
        "indicates off to a side or behind (by name)"
      ],
      [
        "head_flick_(left|right)",
        "directional",
        "flicks the head toward a side (by name)"
